{"agent":"exp3-roadmap-bugs","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The change's stated intent lists the bugs-kind filters as `--status/--since/--limit/--item`, but the kind only declares and implements `filters=frozenset({\"since\", \"limit\", \"status\", \"phase\"})` and reads `f.phase` in `_data` (scoping to `{f.phase} | {t.id for t in q.tasks_under(f.phase)}`). There is no `item` handling anywhere in the file. Concretely, a caller following the documented interface — `export bugs --item T-5` — either gets an unknown/unsupported filter error (since `item` is not among the kind's declared filters and there is no `f.item` read) or, if `item` is parsed by the framework as a generic filter, gets a completely unfiltered bug document, because the only scoping predicate used to build `bugs` is `scope is None or b.item in scope`, and `scope` is only ever populated from `f.phase`. So the requested slice is not produced. Either way the documented `--item` filter has no effect on the emitted bugs, which violates the acceptance requirement that \"filters cut an unfiltered … document to the requested slice.\"","digest":"0b795fa16fc8479f","location":"ddflow/services/export/kind_bugs.py:122 (registry.register for \"bugs\")","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/export/kind_bugs.py:122 (registry.register for \"bugs\")"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"`Log.query(reverse=True)` builds `list(reversed(self.events))` and then immediately throws the order away with `sorted(evs, key=lambda e: e.sort_key())`. Every event in a `Log` gets a distinct lamport (`len(self.events) + 1` in `add`), and the fixture is deliberately built with many events sharing the same timestamp (`_ts(0)`) precisely so that the lamport breaks the ties; consequently the sort key is unique per event and the sort is a total order, i.e. the reversal is a no-op: `g.query(True)` hands the renderer the same event list in the same order as `g.query(False)`. Therefore `assert docs[0] == docs[1] == docs[2]` and `assert a == registry.render_document(\"bugs\", g.query(reverse=True))` are true for *any* implementation, including one that renders in stream order, reuses a stale index across an out-of-order or duplicated feed, or otherwise mishandles event order — exactly the class of bug the \"deterministic across event order\" acceptance criterion exists to catch. (The same vacuity applies to the status test's `registry.render_document(\"status\", q) == registry.render_document(\"status\", q)`, which compares two consecutive calls on the identical input.) A test that can never observe a differently-ordered event stream gives false assurance that ordering is handled.","digest":"032a496da736e43d","location":"tests/test_export_docs_a.py:Log.query (used by `test_roadmap_is_deterministic_across_event_order_and_has_no_clock` and `test_bugs_deterministic_and_markdown_safe`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_export_docs_a.py:Log.query (used by `test_roadmap_is_deterministic_across_event_order_and_has_no_clock` and `test_bugs_deterministic_and_markdown_safe`)"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":27930,"diff_sha":"4c0dbbfaa4581a28b1277870fc3d0d58efc252af09bffdd8ff4d19363bab6755","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-export-docs-bugs-roadmap-status","elapsed_s":866.1,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/export/kind_bugs.py:122 (registry.register for \"bugs\")","tests/test_export_docs_a.py:Log.query (used by `test_roadmap_is_deterministic_across_event_order_and_has_no_clock` and `test_bugs_deterministic_and_markdown_safe`)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"ebfcf37641d35a00f44424b03","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":10221,"schema":1,"subject":"B-export-docs-bugs-roadmap-status","ts":"2026-10-02T14:24:51.453891Z"}
