{"agent":"exp3-roadmap-bugs","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The change drops `OPEN` from the `...core.model` import list, but the rest of the module was not updated to remove `OPEN` from the helpers that still reference it. `_data` builds each phase's rows with `_task_row(q, t)` (line 77 in the new file), and `_task_row` is the helper that derives the `\"ready\"` status — the value `_data` matches for the NEXT lane at `elif any(r[\"status\"] == \"ready\" for r in rows)`. Distinguishing an open-but-unblocked task (which must become `\"ready\"`) from a `BLOCKED`/`RUNNING`/`REVIEW` task requires testing `t.state == OPEN` (or the equivalent membership that includes `OPEN`), so `_task_row`/`waits_on` reference `OPEN`. Concretely, run the export for any roadmap whose query contains one phase with a single `OPEN` task that nothing blocks: `_data` reaches `rows = [_task_row(q, t) ...]`, the helper evaluates the `OPEN` name, and Python raises `NameError: name 'OPEN' is not defined` instead of emitting the NEXT lane. The old body of `open_tasks` was the only *visible* use of `OPEN`, so the author removed the import based on that line alone; the helpers that also need it were left untouched.","digest":"d7312660e73d90e6","location":"ddflow/services/export/kind_roadmap.py:14 (the `...core.model` import) / `_task_row`","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/export/kind_roadmap.py:14 (the `...core.model` import) / `_task_row`"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The reworked fixture no longer reverses the event fold order at all. The old code did\n`sorted(list(reversed(self.events)), key=...)`, which, because `sorted` is stable, flipped the\nrelative order of every event that shares a `sort_key` (very common here: the top of this file\nstamps many events with the same `_ts(day)`, and `bug_log()`/`road_log()` reuse timestamps). The\nnew code sorts `self.events` once, builds the state, and then only rewrites the *insertion order*\nof the already-materialised `st.items` / `st.bugs` dicts. The state's field values are computed\nfrom an identical fold, so the comment \"the same state with every dict in the opposite fold\norder\" is not what the fixture produces — it produces the same fold order with reordered lookup\ndicts.\n\nThis is exactly where the accompanying production change in `kind_status.py` is risky: the\ndocstring now promises agent-hours for an open lease are counted \"up to the newest event in the\nlog\". If that newest-event point is taken from the last event in fold order rather than from\n`max(timestamp)`, reversing the fold (the old fixture) would change the number, but the new\nfixture folds identically, so `docs[0] == docs[2]` cannot detect it. The added assertion\n`list(q.state.items) == list(reversed(list(r.state.items)))` only verifies that the dicts were\nreordered; it does not restore any fold-order coverage. A log with two equal-`sort_key` events\nwhose last-writer-wins resolution differs under reverse fold is a concrete input that now passes\ndeterminism checks it should fail.","digest":"1580e35b3a77488d","location":"tests/test_export_docs_a.py:57 (`Log.query` reverse fixture)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_export_docs_a.py:57 (`Log.query` reverse fixture)"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":9221,"diff_sha":"055b056d3bec7e747537367e57dfc6e4c89f5636e29bbdb49de7a5fd240fc9ed","diff_source":"ef2473f..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-export-docs-bugs-roadmap-status","elapsed_s":760.0,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/export/kind_roadmap.py:14 (the `...core.model` import) / `_task_row`","tests/test_export_docs_a.py:57 (`Log.query` reverse fixture)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e7a821b2eb5f476d9c1b90336","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":10414,"schema":1,"subject":"B-export-docs-bugs-roadmap-status","ts":"2026-10-02T14:47:20.769074Z"}
